===persian===

در فاصله دریا و جنگل
زنی را دوست دارم...
در هر بمباران به جنگل پناه می‌برم
تا در آغوشش...
به دریا بیاندیشم...

اصفهان ۱۳۶۷/۲/۱۶

===machine===

In the distance between the sea and the jungle
There is a woman I love...
During every bombardment, I take refuge in the jungle
So that in her embrace...
I can think of the sea...

Isfahan 1367/2/16

===lantern===

In the gap between sea and forest
lives a woman I love...
Each time the bombs come, I flee into the forest —
so that, held in her arms,
I can think of the sea...

Isfahan, 1367/2/16

===translation===

In the distance between the sea and the forest
there is a woman I love...
At every bombardment I take refuge in the forest,
so that, in her arms,
I may think of the sea...

— Isfahan, 1367/2/16

===footnotes===

جنگل (jangal) is rendered "forest" rather than "jungle": Jafari's recurring war-poem image is the wooded Caspian littoral, a place of refuge between the mountains and the sea. The same sea/forest pairing returns in the page-65 poem ("still the forest is bound to the sea"). The dateline places this in Isfahan, spring 1367 (May 1988), in the closing months of the Iran–Iraq war.
